# SIM baseline: 7" (2807, 7x3.5 two-blade, 4S 5000). PX4 v1.17, Gazebo Harmonic, 2026-11-04.
# Load on top of the airframe defaults. Lines starting with # are notes and QGC skips them.
# Vehicle-Id Component-Id Name Value Type
# Rate gains from the Day 4 gain sweep (step_tests.py + analyze_steps.py)
# MC_ROLLRATE_K: taken from the 6S sweep: smooth at 0.85, shook at 1.0, so about half the shake point.
#   The 4S drone never shook in its sweep, even at 1.0, so on 4S this is on the careful side
1	1	MC_ROLLRATE_K	0.5	9
# MC_PITCHRATE_K: same as roll; checked with the pitch step
1	1	MC_PITCHRATE_K	0.5	9
# MPC_THR_HOVER: the hover thrust PX4 learned in sim (hover_thrust_estimate)
1	1	MPC_THR_HOVER	0.39	9
# NAV_DLL_ACT: ground-station link lost: do nothing. Same in the real-drone file: the RC link is the safety link, not Wi-Fi
1	1	NAV_DLL_ACT	0	6
# Motion limits from P3's perception requirements (docs/PERCEPTION_REQUIREMENTS.md)
# MPC_XY_VEL_MAX: v_max 1.5 m/s
1	1	MPC_XY_VEL_MAX	1.5	9
# MPC_XY_CRUISE: normal autonomous speed 1.0 m/s. Below PX4's listed minimum of 3, so QGC flags it: expected
1	1	MPC_XY_CRUISE	1.0	9
# MPC_VEL_MANUAL: same cap when a person flies in Position mode. Also below the listed minimum of 3: expected
1	1	MPC_VEL_MANUAL	1.5	9
# MPC_ACC_HOR: braking 2 m/s^2, the number P3 used for stopping distance
1	1	MPC_ACC_HOR	2.0	9
# Failsafes. Team spec: return-home and low-battery failsafes.
# Return needs a global position. With no GPS PX4 cannot run it and drops to Land by itself
# (commander/failsafe/framework.cpp: case RTL falls through to case Land).
# NAV_RCL_ACT: RC lost -> Return (Land when there is no GPS)
1	1	NAV_RCL_ACT	2	6
# COM_LOW_BAT_ACT: Return at critical battery, land at emergency
1	1	COM_LOW_BAT_ACT	3	6
# RTL_RETURN_ALT: default is 60 m. Indoors that flies into the ceiling. P3's max height is 3 m
1	1	RTL_RETURN_ALT	2.5	9
# RTL_DESCEND_ALT: default is 30 m, same reason
1	1	RTL_DESCEND_ALT	2.0	9
# BAT_LOW_THR: warning at 25%
1	1	BAT_LOW_THR	0.25	9
# BAT_CRIT_THR: critical (Return) at 15%
1	1	BAT_CRIT_THR	0.15	9
# BAT_EMERGEN_THR: emergency (Land) at 7%
1	1	BAT_EMERGEN_THR	0.07	9
# COM_OF_LOSS_T: offboard link timeout: no setpoints from the ROS 2 node for 0.5 s counts as offboard lost (PX4 default 1 s).
#   This is NOT P3's P-11a (depth older than 0.5 s -> hover). PX4 never sees the depth data, so if the node keeps
#   sending while depth is stale, PX4 can't tell. P-11a has to live in P2's offboard node
1	1	COM_OF_LOSS_T	0.5	9
# COM_OBL_RC_ACT: offboard lost -> Land. In offboard, a lost position estimate also counts as offboard lost
#   (HealthAndArmingChecks/checks/offboardCheck.cpp), so this also lands on flow loss (P3's P-11b),
#   but only while the node sends position or velocity setpoints: offboardCheck.cpp only checks the estimate that
#   setpoint type needs. With attitude or rate setpoints a flow loss is not caught here.
#   With no position PX4 falls through to Descend (failsafe/framework.cpp). The pilot can take over with the mode switch
1	1	COM_OBL_RC_ACT	4	6
# EKF2_NOAID_TOUT: flow drone: declare position lost after 1 s without flow, not 5 s (in microseconds)
1	1	EKF2_NOAID_TOUT	1000000	6
